error[SC0402]: this may use `p` after it was freed
   ╭─[ a_definition_s_lengths_are_found_after_another_definition.c:7:31 ]
   │
 7 │ int f(int * _Nonnull p, int b[*p], int a[(free(p), 1)]) {
   │                               ─┬          ───┬───  
   │                                ╰─────────────────── used here, perhaps after the free
   │                                              │     
   │                                              ╰───── freed here
───╯
  = note: C17 6.7.6 p3 puts a sequence point at the end of a full declarator, and a parameter's declarator is not one, so nothing orders one parameter's length against another's, and this check found nothing here that orders the free before this
  = note: this check belongs to safety level 1
  = note: this could not be proven, and unproven results are errors in this compilation
  = help: free it in the body instead, where every parameter's length has already been evaluated
